From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kiritake Kumi <root@niconiconi.us>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: enable the WiFi SDIO slot on LicheeRV
 Nano B

The WiFi chip of the board (a plain AIC8800, revision U03) sits on the
second SDHCI controller, SD1. The vendor u-boot already powers the chip
(GPIOA26 pulse, kept high) and muxes the SD1 pads before the kernel
starts, so the controller only needs to be enabled: no mmc-pwrseq and no
pin config here, the pads come out of reset in the SD1 function.

The frequency stays at 25 MHz like in the vendor device tree, whose
wifi-sd node runs the slot at 25 MHz even though the driver asks for 50.

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts
index 5f7c2160a..8b9d3f1c2 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts
@@ -94,10 +94,23 @@ &uart0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&sdhci1 {
+	bus-width = <4>;
+	cap-sdio-irq;
+	cap-sd-highspeed;
+	keep-power-in-suspend;
+	no-1-8-v;
+	no-mmc;
+	no-sd;
+	non-removable;
+	max-frequency = <25000000>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &gmac0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &mdio {
 	status = "okay";
 };
